  "content": {
    "title": "Grammys 2026 Winners List: Bad Bunny, Kendrick Lamar, Olivia Dean and More",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTA complete rundown of the artists, albums, songs and videos that took home trophies at the 68th annual awards.Listen · 13:31 min Bad Bunny won the night’s final prize, album of the year.Credit...Kevin Winter/Getty ImagesFeb. 1, 2026The 68th annual Grammy Awards were the first in more than a decade without a showdown involving Taylor Swift, Beyoncé or Adele. But history was still made: Kendrick Lamar turned five of his nine nominations (including record of the year) into wins, making him the most awarded rapper in the show’s history. Bad Bunny, who will headline the Super Bowl halftime show next weekend, became the first to win album of the year with a Spanish-language LP. Billie Eilish and Finneas are now the first to win song of the year three times. And “Golden” from “KPop Demon Hunters” took best song written for visual media, earning K-pop its first ever Grammy.The awards honored recordings released from Aug. 31, 2024, through Aug. 30, 2025, across 95 categories. Catch up on our live coverage here.ImageOlivia Dean said she was on the Grammy stage “as a granddaughter of an immigrant.”Credit...Valerie Macon/Agence France-Presse — Getty ImagesA correction was made onFeb. 2, 2026: An earlier version of this article misspelled the name of the musician who won best rock performance. It is Yungblud, not Yungblood.A version of this article appears in print on Feb. 3, 2026, Section C, Page 5 of the New York edition with the headline: 2026 Grammy Winners. Order Reprints | Today’s Paper | SubscribeAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
